  (:adr/body "# Drone manufacturing: the gap was one rotor solver, not a platform

## What was asked

\"drone, USV, 車載用 OS, drone OS, 防衛用 OS, lib は kotoba で設計実装済み?\" —
then \"では設計実装, drone 製造から\".

## What already existed (measured 2026-08-29/30, not estimated)

Against 4,264 west projects:

- `kotoba-lang/kami-autodrive` (src 39 / test 26) — vehicle-class-agnostic GNC,
  with FOUR plants already implemented: bicycle, ship-hydro (Fossen 3-DOF),
  fixed-wing and multirotor. The autonomy layer for drones was not missing.
- `kotoba-lang/swarm-choreo` (src 10 / test 5), `kotoba-lang/robotics`
  (mission / action / governor, \"policy, not control\"), `org-ros`, `org-ros-urdf`.
- `kotoba-lang/kami-engine-motor` — reduced-order traction motor, air-gap shear
  sizing, with an INVERSE `size-for-power`.
- `kotoba-lang/kami-engine-aero` (automotive Cd), `kami-engine-echem` (PEM fuel
  cell), `kami-engine-cae-solver` (the `cae.solver/solve` dispatch contract),
  `kami-engine-vehicle-designer` (DesignProposer sealed behind a PhysicsGovernor
  that closes the mass spiral and REJECTS designs that do not converge).
- `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-3030` — aerospace manufacturing actor
  (assembly intake, NDT screening, airworthiness evidence). It contains zero
  occurrences of uav / drone / unmanned: it is manned-aerospace assembly.
- `gftdcojp/defence` (src 16 / test 8) — BOM explosion, supply-chain risk
  propagation, ITAR/USML + EAR/ECCN export classification, contract lifecycle,
  keccak-256 audit receipts. Procurement and export control, no weapons.
- `cloud-itonami/drone` — DESIGN ONLY, and the repo says so itself: the host is
  NXDOMAIN, there is no component.wasm, and the appview does not build.

## The gap

Sizing a multirotor runs `thrust -> rotor -> motor -> pack`. The second arrow
had no solver. `motor.solver/size-for-power` takes a peak-kW target; nothing in
the workspace computed what that target should be for a rotorcraft. Every
kami-engine solver is automotive or fuel-cell; none of them turns thrust into a
disc.

That is one namespace-sized hole, not a platform-sized one. Building a \"drone
platform\" before filling it would have produced another `cloud-itonami/drone`.

## Decision

Create `kotoba-lang/kami-engine-rotor` — a reduced-order rotor solver
registering `:rom-rotor` on the existing `cae.solver` contract, as a sibling of
kami-engine-motor / -aero / -echem, in portable zero-dep `.cljc`.

`size-for-thrust` produces exactly the case `motor.solver/size-for-power`
consumes, so the chain closes without either repo learning about the other.

### Two power models, held against each other

- `hover`   : P = T*vi / FM (momentum theory + figure of merit)
- `forward` : P = k_i*T*vi + P_profile*(1 + 4.65*mu^2), vi from Glauert

`forward` degrades to the hover decomposition at mu = 0, so `hover` also reports
`:fm-implied` — the FM the decomposed model implies at the same operating point.
A caller passing an `:fm` far from `:fm-implied` has two models disagreeing
about one rotor, and the disagreement is on the result map rather than averaged
away. A test pins that they agree to 1e-9 at mu = 0.

### Refusals are explicit

Following the repo-wide rule that a check which could not run must not return
the value of a check that ran and found nothing: non-positive thrust / diameter
/ RPM throw with the offending `:key` in ex-data rather than returning NaN;
altitude outside the ISA troposphere throws rather than extrapolating a
lapse-rate law that has stopped applying; blade stall above CT/sigma = 0.12 is
reported as `:stalled? true` rather than returned as arithmetic.

## Evidence

20 tests / 69 assertions, green under both `clojure -M:dev:test` (local
siblings) and `clojure -M:test` (git deps — the path the fleet gate takes).
clj-kondo: 0 errors, 0 warnings.

Every expected value was computed by hand from the governing equation BEFORE the
code was run. Reference rotor: 15-inch two-blade prop, 10 N at sea level,
5000 rpm -> 92.05 W shaft, 11.08 g/W, 0.176 N*m, tip Mach 0.293, CT/sigma 0.090,
22.6 g of blade. The 11.08 g/W and the 22.6 g both land inside the published
range for real 15-inch carbon props, which is the only external check available.

Verified DISCRIMINATING by breaking it three ways and confirming the reported
failure matched the break:

| break | result |
|---|---|
| `P = T*vi * FM` instead of `/ FM` | 6 tests red |
| drop `(1 + 4.65*mu^2)` from profile power | 3 red, named `forward-flight-has-a-power-bucket` and `forward-flight-relieves-the-rotor` |
| pin density to sea level, ignoring altitude | 2 tests red |

Restoring each returned 0 failures.

Two tests failed on the first run and both failures were real:

1. A float equality on tip speed — the TEST was wrong (rpm is derived from tip
   speed and tip speed recomputed from rpm, so they differ in the last ULP).
2. `profile-power-eventually-wins` asserted cruise power climbs back above HOVER
   power at 45 m/s. It does not, and the assertion was wrong physics, not a bug:
   for this disc loading the crossover sits near mu = 0.95, far outside the
   model's valid range. Replaced with the claim that IS true and IS
   discriminating — an interior power bucket (P(30) < P(20) and P(30) < P(45)),
   which requires both terms to be present.

## What this does NOT do

Stated plainly so the next reader does not inherit an overclaim:

- **No pack/battery solver exists in this workspace.** `kami-engine-echem` is a
  PEM fuel cell, not Li-ion. Endurance is therefore NOT computable end-to-end
  today. A pack solver would register its own kind on the same contract.
- **No multirotor mass closure.** `vdesign.physics/close-mass` is car-shaped and
  lives inside the vehicle-designer app, not in a shared lib. The drone spiral
  (thrust = weight, so mass appears on both sides) is not written yet.
- **No design actor, no manufacturing vertical, no compliance surface.** Nothing
  here does BOM, serialisation, remote ID, 機体認証 or export classification for
  UAS. `gftdcojp/defence` has the export-control classifier that such a vertical
  would call; they are not wired together.
- **One rotor in isolation.** No rotor-on-rotor interference, no ground effect,
  no airframe parasite drag. Above roughly mu = 0.5 the edgewise model is out of
  range and does not say so.

## Registration

- GitHub: kotoba-lang/kami-engine-rotor (public, per repos.edn :orgs :visibility)
- west: `manifest/repos.edn` :extra-projects + single-entry
  `gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry kami-engine-rotor`; pin verified reachable from
  the default branch by `verify-west-pins`.
- CI: fleet gate `{:name \"kami-engine-rotor\" :gate :jvm-test :ship-git-deps true}`
  in `scripts/fleet-ci/gates.edn`. NO `.github/workflows` was written
  (ADR-2607300900: CI/CD is murakumo fleet, not GitHub Actions).
  Per the repo-wide rule, this gate is NOT landed until it has been green on the
  fleet once; it has not run there yet.

## Next slice

In order, each a separate decision:

1. A Li-ion pack solver (`:rom-pack`) on the same contract — specific energy,
   usable DoD, C-rate sag. Without it endurance stays uncomputable.
2. The multirotor mass closure as a shared governor: payload + endurance ->
   MTOW fixed point, DIVERGENCE AS THE REJECT SIGNAL, mirroring
   `vdesign.physics/close-mass`.
3. Only then a UAS design/manufacturing vertical, and only if it can name what
   it refuses the way isic-8422 does.
")))
